{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-50-1","title":"Jeremiah 50:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":50,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":50,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The judgment of Babylon and the redemption of Israel.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3409. B.C. 595. against Babylon. 25:26,27; 27:7; 51:1-14; Ps 137:8,9; Isa 13:1-3; 14:4; 21:1-10 Isa 47:1-15; Hab 2:5-20; Re 18:1-24 the land. Ge 11:31; Job 1:17; Isa 23:13; Ac 7:4 Jeremiah. Heb. the hand of Jeremiah 2Sa 23:2; 2Pe 1:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-50-2","title":"Jeremiah 50:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":50,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":50,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Declare. 6:18; 31:10; 46:14; Ps 64:9; 96:3; Isa 12:4; 48:6; 66:18,19 Re 14:6-8 set up. Heb. lift up. Isa 13:2 Babylon. 51:8; Isa 21:9; Re 14:8; 18:2 Bel. 51:44; Isa 46:1 Merodach. 52:31; Isa 39:1 her idols. 46; 43:12,13; Isa 37:19; Zep 2:11 Xerxes, after his return from his unsuccessful expedition into Greece, partly out of religious zeal, being a professed enemy to image worship, and partly to reimburse himself after his immense expenses, seized the sacred treasures, and plundered or destroyed the temples and idols of Babylon, thereby accomplishing the prophecies of Isaiah and Jeremiah. (Isa 21:9; 46:1. Jer 50:2; 51:44, 47, 52.) What God declares, \"I will punish Bel in Babylon, and I will bring forth that which he has swallowed,\" was also literally fulfilled, when the vessels of the house of God, which Nebuchadnezzar had brought from Jerusalem and placed in the temple of Bel, Da 1:2, were restored by order of Cyrus, Ezr 1:7, and again carried to Jerusalem. Bp. Newton, Dis. X.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-50-3","title":"Jeremiah 50:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":50,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":50,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>out of the.The Medes, who formed the greatest part of the army of Cyrus. Media lay N.E. of Babylon.</p>\n<p>9,41; 51:11,27,48; Isa 13:5,17,18,20 which. 12,13,35-40; 51:8,9,25,26,37-44,62; Isa 13:6-10,19-22; 14:22-24 Re 18:21-23 both. 7:20; 21:6; Ge 6:7; Ex 12:12; Zep 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-50-4","title":"Jeremiah 50:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":50,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":50,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>those. 20; 3:16-18; 33:15; 51:47,48; Isa 63:4 the children of Israel. 19,20,33,34; 3:18; 33:6-8; 30:10,11; 31:6,7,31; 33:7; Isa 11:12,13 Isa 14:1; Eze 37:16-22; 39:25; Ho 1:11 going. 31:9,10; Ezr 3:12,13; Ps 126:4-6; Joe 2:12; Zec 12:10; Jas 4:9 seek the. 29:12-14; Ps 105:4; Isa 45:19; 55:6; Ho 3:5; Zec 8:21-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-50-5","title":"Jeremiah 50:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":50,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":50,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>ask. 6:16; Ps 25:8,9; 84:7; Isa 35:8; Joh 7:17 Come. 31:31-36; Isa 2:3-5; Mic 4:1,2; Ac 11:23; 2Co 8:5 in a. 32:40; Ge 17:7; 2Sa 23:5; Isa 55:3; 56:6,7 that shall. 32:40; 1Ki 19:10,14; Heb 8:6-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-50-6","title":"Jeremiah 50:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":50,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":50,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>people. 17; Ps 119:176; Isa 53:6; Mt 9:36; 10:6; 15:24; 18:11-13; Lu 15:4-7 1Pe 2:25 their shepherds. 10:21; 23:11-15; Isa 56:10-12; Eze 34:4-12; Zec 11:4-9 on the. 2:20; 3:6,23; Eze 34:6 have forgotten. 2:32; Ps 32:7; 90:1; 91:1; 116:7; Isa 30:15; 32:2 resting place. Heb. place to lie down in. Ps 23:2; So 1:7,8; Eze 34:14,25-28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-50-7","title":"Jeremiah 50:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":50,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":50,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>have devoured. 17,33; 12:7-11; Ps 79:7; Isa 9:12; 56:9 We offend. 2:3; 40:2,3; Isa 47:6; Da 9:6,16; Zec 1:15; 11:5 the habitation. 31:23; Ps 90:1; 91:1 the hope. 14:8; Ps 22:4,5; 1Ti 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-50-8","title":"Jeremiah 50:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","ref